 defense-in-depth) -- add a DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check to
 scripts/adversarial_verify.py. The .396 ARC-GEN cross-generator result
 (exp4282) reported a perfect cross_family_delta=1.0 CI[1.0,1.0] that was a
 CONSTRUCTION ARTIFACT (wrong-majority-only pool -> vote@1=0.0;
 trivially-separable -> set_encoder@1=1.0), and adversarial_verify.py did NOT
 flag it -- it was caught only by a manual outer-loop audit
 (docs/research-notes/exp4282-arcgen-degenerate-audit-2026-06-16.md). Add a
 mechanical DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check: flag (CRITICAL) when a
 beats-vote/selection delta >= ~0.95 AND the baseline (vote_at_1 /
 matched_control) <= ~0.05, OR when oracle_at_k == 1.0 with a perfect
 selector. Add a unit test that the check NOW flags exp4282's artifact AND
 does NOT flag the genuine .395 win (exp4271, vote 0.25 / verifier 0.69). This
 is the safety net that prevents recurrence of the .396 degenerate-pool waste
 (Phase prototype + adversarial check discipline). Deliverable = the patched
 linter + a passing test. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.

Automated research step by research conductor.
